For the Ca–EDTA formation equilibrium:

\[
\text{Ca}^{2+}+\text{Y}^{4-}\rightleftharpoons \text{CaY}^{2-}
\qquad
K_f=\frac{[\text{CaY}^{2-}]}{[\text{Ca}^{2+}][\text{Y}^{4-}]}=5\times10^{10}
\]

Starting with 0.020 M stoichiometric Ca–EDTA complex, let \(x\) dissociate:

\[
[\text{Ca}^{2+}]=[\text{Y}^{4-}]=x,\quad [\text{CaY}^{2-}]=0.020-x
\]

Since \(K_f\) is very large, \(x\ll 0.020\), so:

\[
5\times10^{10}\approx \frac{0.020}{x^2}
\]

\[
x=\sqrt{\frac{0.020}{5\times10^{10}}}
=\sqrt{4.0\times10^{-13}}
=6.3\times10^{-7}\text{ M}
\]

Answer: D
